sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-carmona-neural-crest-chase-and-run> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-carmona-neural-crest-chase-and-run-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-carmona-neural-crest-chase-and-run-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Carmona-Fontaine et al. (2008, 2011) & Theveneau et al. (2013) neural crest CIL, C3a co-attraction & Sdf1 chase-and-run migration — MorphoEval overall 90.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2012-carmona-neural-crest-chase-and-run.py` (91.1/100, up from 57.6/100 in Pass 1; +33.5 overall). The remediated script simulates all 5 experimental perturbation regimes of Theveneau et al. (2013) (`wildtype_chase_and_run` FMI = 0.6853, `stationary_sdf1_bead` FMI = 0.4220, `ncad_dshdep_no_cil` FMI = 0.2899, `c3ar_morpholino_no_coa` FMI = 0.2191, and `placode_ablated_no_sdf1` FMI = 0.0080), achieving Pearson r = 0.9954 (RMSE = 0.0269) against empirical FMI and r = 0.9779 against 6-hour collective displacement, models the 3 cranial neural crest streams (`r4`, `r6`, `r7`) chasing epibranchial placodes (`e1`, `e2`, `e3`) between Semaphorin-3F repulsive pharyngeal pouches (`p1`, `p2`, `p3`), and segments `neural_crest_specimen.jpg` across Control Panel A and BMPR-inhibited Panel C (dorsoventral separation +0.4063, inter-placode spacing CV = 0.0457, profile r = 0.9225), backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_091_neural_crest_chase_and_run.lean`. Overall 90.9/100 (faithfulness 90.7, reproducibility 91.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/neural_crest_chase_and_run_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-carmona-neural-crest-chase-and-run.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 502131 B, 3075×1290 px, artifact_sha256 2d76edf0601f4cce565372ca0c48bb0594630a6bd4ea51b00401b33e0803e22f (sha256 2d76edf0601f4cce565372ca0c48bb0594630a6bd4ea51b00401b33e0803e22f), spec_fingerprint eaab4129b9e5439c62a3183cca6415d43a158fd3cba206648d80e37937887881. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eaab4129b9e5439c62a3183cca6415d43a158fd3cba206648d80e37937887881; artifact_sha256: 2d76edf0601f4cce565372ca0c48bb0594630a6bd4ea51b00401b33e0803e22f. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-neural-crest-chase-and-run-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Theveneau et al. (2013) Nat. Cell Biol. 15:763-772 five-regime chase-and-run hierarchy across wild-type NC + placode (FMI = 0.68, 6h disp = 185 um), stationary Sdf1 bead (FMI = 0.42, disp = 95 um), N-cadherin/DshDep+ CIL blockade (FMI = 0.28, disp = 54 um), C3aR-MO COA ablation (FMI = 0.21, disp = 38 um), and placode/Sdf1 ablation (FMI = 0.04, disp = 12 um) | Carmona-Fontaine et al. (2008, 2011) and Woods et al. (2014) PLOS ONE 9:e104969 short-range PCP/RhoA contact inhibition of locomotion (CIL) and autocrine C3a/C3aR co-attraction (COA) stabilizing collective cluster migration; reconstructed_in_script: 2D interacting multi-agent chase-and-run dynamical system across all 5 experimental regimes of Theveneau et al. (2013) (FMI Pearson r = 0.9954, RMSE = 0.0269; 6h displacement Pearson r = 0.9779) plus 3-stream pharyngeal arch simulation (r4, r6, r7 streams targeting e1, e2, e3 placodes between pharyngeal pouches p1-p3) | Automated segmentation of neural_crest_specimen.jpg (Panel A control vs Panel C BMPR-inhibited) quantifying dorsoventral chaser-runner separation (+0.4063), inter-placode spacing CV (0.0457), BMPR ventral stream loss (0.5877), and dorsoventral density profile correlation (r = 0.9225, RMSE = 0.2640); transfer_boundary: 2D planar agent-based cranial neural crest and epibranchial placode migration mapped to whole-embryo 3D cranial stream reconstructions; does_not_claim: Subcellular actin-myosin vertex mechanics or 3D cranial neural tube delamination prior to neural crest EMT." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend the 2D planar cranial stream model to a 3D curved pharyngeal arch manifold incorporating neural crest proliferation and extracellular matrix fibronectin remodeling." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.909"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

